If `count` is provided and is larger than `packed.len() * 16`, the loop will attempt to access `packed[word]` where `word >= packed.len()`, causing an out-of-bounds panic. Clamping `total` to `packed.len() * TERNARY_VALUES_PER_WORD` prevents any potential out-of-bounds panics.

```suggestion
pub fn unpack_ternary(packed: &[u32], count: Option<usize>) -> Vec<i8> {
    let total = count
        .unwrap_or(packed.len() * TERNARY_VALUES_PER_WORD)
        .min(packed.len() * TERNARY_VALUES_PER_WORD);
    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(total);
    for i in 0..total {
        let word = i / TERNARY_VALUES_PER_WORD;
        let bit = (i % TERNARY_VALUES_PER_WORD) * 2;
        let code = (packed[word] >> bit) & 0b11;
        let val = match code {
            0b01 => 1i8,
            0b10 => -1i8,
            _ => 0i8, // 0b00 and 0b11 both decode to 0
        };
        out.push(val);
    }
    out
}
```

