If the user passes `--iterations 0` via the command line, the benchmark runner will attempt to access `durations[0]` and `durations[iterations - 1]` in `run_benchmark`, resulting in an out-of-bounds panic. Adding a validation check to ensure `iterations > 0` prevents this crash.

```suggestion
                "--iterations" | "-n" => {
                    i += 1;
                    iterations = args[i].parse().expect("--iterations requires a number");
                    if iterations == 0 {
                        eprintln!("Error: --iterations must be greater than 0");
                        std::process::exit(1);
                    }
                }
```

